# plasma — candidate palette, same derivation as cool.env:
# matplotlib's `plasma` colormap sampled at t = 0, .25, .5, .75, 1 and
# pastelised toward white at strength 0.68; the alert pair at 0.25. The dark
# neutrals carry the ramp's own hue so the palette reads as one family.
COOL_BG0=#22151A
COOL_BG1=#36252C
COOL_BG2=#4B353D
COOL_FG0=#FBF2F6
COOL_FG1=#EFC4D4
COOL_DIM=#E8ACC2
COOL_DIMMER=#E39AB5
COOL_0=#B2B0D8
COOL_1=#D6AEE3
COOL_2=#EFC4D4
COOL_3=#FDDDC2
COOL_4=#FAFDB8
COOL_HOT_0=#4945A5
COOL_HOT_4=#F4FA59
COOL_MINT=#D6AEE3
COOL_BLUSH=#FDDDC2
COOL_ACCENT=#B2B0D8
COOL_ACTIVE=#4945A5
COOL_URGENT=#F4FA59
COOL_WARN=#FDDDC2
COOL_GOOD=#D6AEE3
COOL_INACTIVE=#4B353D
